{{if temporal}}
| `cmd/worker/` | The worker's command |
{{end}}
| `*_test.go` | The tests |

## Change it

After a change in `project/`, check it and make the code again:

```sh
ritsu check project
go generate ./...
go test ./...
```

| What to change | Where | How |
|---|---|---|
| The rules of a request | `project/*.ringi` | [Change the request type]({{site}}change/) |
| A new kind of request | A new file `project/<name>.ringi` | [Add and change request types]({{site}}types/) |
| The people and the teams | `project/org/` | [Prepare the organization's data]({{site}}organization/) |
| The business days and the holidays | `project/shared/office.cal` | [Set the business days]({{site}}calendar/) |
| Who may do what | `project/shared/company.gate` | [Decide who may do what]({{site}}permissions/) |
| How notices are sent | `notify.go` | [Send the notices by mail]({{site}}mail/) |
| What is left of a budget or of days of leave | A new file `project/shared/<name>.book` | [Check budgets and days of leave]({{site}}books/) |
| Work after an approval, such as a payment | A file `project/shared/<name>.flow` | [Start work after an approval]({{site}}flows/) |

Once people use a request type, raise its version before you change its rules, so that the requests in
progress end by the rules they were made under ([how]({{site}}types/#change-the-rules-of-a-type-in-use)).

## The tests

`go test ./...` runs {{test_count}} tests.

| Test | What it sees |
|---|---|
| `TestVectors` | That the server does what the rules and the examples say. It gives the server every operation ritsu made from them (`requests/vectors/`), and compares what comes back |
| `TestGate` | That `gate.go` answers rightly what each person may do, by role and department |
| `TestPages` | That a request can be made and approved on the pages |
{{if mcp}}
| `TestTools` | That an agent can make a purchase request with the tools and read it, and that a request with no one signed in is answered 401 |
{{end}}
{{if temporal}}
| `TestFlows` | That the payment of an approved expense claim runs on Temporal's server for development, with the workers of `cmd/worker`: the requester is paid once, and told. It uses the Temporal CLI that `TEMPORAL_CLI` names, else the file the SDK keeps in the system's temporary directory (`temporal-cli-go-sdk-<version>`). Without either it prints `SKIP`, and downloads nothing |
{{end}}

[Test it]({{site}}testing/) says how to test the parts you write, and what to run in CI.

## Run it for your staff

A server your staff use keeps the requests in PostgreSQL, signs people in with your organization's
sign-in, and takes https. [Prepare it and start it]({{site}}operations/) says what to prepare and how to
start it. `go run ./cmd/server -h` lists the flags.
{{if temporal}}

Give the server and each worker the address of your Temporal with `-temporal <host:port>`. The
namespace and TLS are the client's options (`client.Options`) in `cmd/server/main.go` and
`cmd/worker/main.go`.
{{end}}

Started with no sign-in at all, the server takes a request as that of the person in its header
`X-Person`. That header and `-dev-login` check no one. The server takes them on this computer only,
refuses a request a proxy forwarded, and does not start with them beside `-tls-cert` or the settings
of a sign-in.
